        "id": 8515,
        "name": "Krayden006",
        "username": "Krayden006",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/krayden006/{size}/2414_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-08-12T16:16:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>This question/argument has come up a couple times with a member of my gaming group.&nbsp; I can't remember the exact card or wording but any card that targets the hero with the most ongoings in play or the most anything else will do.&nbsp; The argument is if more than one hero has the same amount of ongoings in play, then&nbsp;no one&nbsp;has the most, therefore said card affects no one.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Being that I own the cards, the first time this came up I said no and we decided as a group who would take the negative effect.&nbsp; The second time it was&nbsp;brought it up, we all had zero ongoings in play so I decided we would all take the effects of the card.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Just looking for a little clarification.&nbsp; Something in writing that I can show.</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:39:03.950Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
        "quote_count": 0,
        "incoming_link_count": 1,
        "reads": 0,
        "readers_count": 0,
        "score": 5.0,
        "yours": false,
        "topic_id": 8512,
        "topic_slug": "cards-that-target-heroes-with-the-most",
